# Webhook Gateway Architecture Rules

## CRITICAL: Technology Stack Constraints
- Always use FastStream, never suggest or implement Celery
- Use async/await for all database operations and API endpoints
- Development uses SQLite + FakeRedis, production uses MySQL + Redis
- All new code must use uv for dependency management

## File Organization Rules
- API endpoints: place in [app/api/v1/endpoints/](mdc:app/api/v1/endpoints/)
- Database models: modify [app/db/models.py](mdc:app/db/models.py)
- Event handlers: add to [app/stream/handlers.py](mdc:app/stream/handlers.py)
- Configuration: update [app/core/config.py](mdc:app/core/config.py)

## DEPRECATED - Do Not Use
- Never modify files in [app/worker/](mdc:app/worker) (Celery legacy)
- Never use [app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest.py](mdc:app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest.py)
- Always use [app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest_faststream.py](mdc:app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest_faststream.py) for webhook ingestion

## FastStream Event Pattern
When implementing webhook processing:
1. Use `@broker.subscriber("queue.name")` decorators
2. Publish events with `await broker.publish(data, "queue.name")`
3. All handlers run in the same process as FastAPI
4. Import broker from [app/stream/app.py](mdc:app/stream/app.py)

## Database Rules
- Always use async SQLAlchemy sessions
- Import session from [app/db/session.py](mdc:app/db/session.py)
- Use soft deletes for subscriptions (set `is_active=False`)
- Store raw webhook payloads as LONGTEXT, not JSON

## Authentication Rules
- Management APIs require Bearer token from `API_KEY` config
- Use `Depends(verify_api_key)` for protected endpoints
- Webhook endpoints verify HMAC signatures from source secrets
